ssh-gate (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Tunnel names now always resolve inside the tunnel. TUNNEL_DNS lists DNS
    servers queried over TCP through the tunnel, default 1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8;
    127.0.0.53 is the resolver of the VPS itself.
  * DOH_HOST is optional and off by default. Setting it and TUNNEL_DNS
    together is a startup error. Upgrade note: an unset DOH_HOST no longer
    means cloudflare-dns.com, and an empty one no longer sends tunnel names
    to the local resolver; both now use the TUNNEL_DNS servers. A value kept
    in /etc/default/ssh-gate stays in effect.
  * Names matching a domain or re: rule use only the local resolver: these
    rules are now checked before ip: rules, whatever their order.
  * LOCAL_DNS_ON_NXDOMAIN=on|off (default off) asks the local resolver after
    a tunnel not-found, for names only the local network knows. A local
    answer of only private addresses then goes direct, except loopback and
    link-local, and is refused while the tunnel is up but no tunnel resolver
    answers.
  * The tunnel step of a lookup has its own 3 s bound, so a silent server
    leaves the local resolver time to answer; before, that lookup failed.
  * A tunnel resolver no channel opens to is paused for 10 s, then one lookup
    probes it. A failure on an open channel is about the name and pauses
    nothing, so a web page cannot switch the resolvers off.
  * /api/status has a dns field and the Web UI a DNS row: latency, failed
    lookups, fallbacks to the local resolver.

 -- Nikita Kozlov <niakrisn@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:02:24 +0000

ssh-gate (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * systemd: Type=notify. READY=1 once the listeners are open (not waiting
    for the tunnel); the Status: line of systemctl status shows the tunnel
    state: not configured, connecting, key not accepted, unreachable, host
    key changed, SSH error, connected, reconnecting, stopping. A failure
    state names the file to act on and the next retry.
  * Empty SSH_HOST or SSH_USER is no longer fatal: the service runs with the
    proxies off, health and Web UI only. The package now starts the service
    on a fresh install.
  * Startup errors exit with 78; RestartPreventExitStatus=78 keeps the unit
    failed instead of restarting it in a loop.
  * /api/status reports ssh.state and ssh.error; /readyz names the state;
    the Web UI shows it.
  * Logs go to journald over its native protocol: a priority per line,
    identifiers ssh-gate and ssh-gate-access. Outside systemd both stay JSON
    on stderr.
  * ACCESS_LOG=on|off (default on), not affected by LOG_LEVEL. Access lines
    carry conn_id and result; the error is a service log warning with the
    same conn_id.
  * LogRateLimitBurst=50000 per 30 s; /etc/rsyslog.d/40-ssh-gate.conf keeps
    the access log out of the syslog files.

 -- Nikita Kozlov <niakrisn@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:21:31 +0000

ssh-gate (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security: check the SSH host key on every reconnect, not only at
    startup. A TOFU-trusted key was not pinned for the rest of the process,
    so a reconnect accepted any host key and overwrote ssh_known_hosts.
    A connect that cannot save the key now fails.
  * Security: update golang.org/x/crypto to v0.58.0 and the Go toolchain to
    1.26.10 (SSH client panics and deadlocks, net/http and crypto/x509
    fixes); pin the build images.
  * Security: refuse tunnel destinations whose addresses are all private or
    loopback, so the VPS is never asked to dial its own network. Classify
    IPv4-mapped and zoned address literals, 0.0.0.0/8, 100.64.0.0/10 and
    fc00::/7 as private.
  * Privacy: ip: rules are matched on the DoH answer; deciding a route no
    longer sends every destination name to the local resolver.
  * Web UI: answer only to allowed Host names (DNS rebinding guard), new
    UI_ALLOWED_HOSTS; add nosniff, frame and CSP headers.
  * HTTP proxy: limit request headers to 1 MiB (431 above), replace the
    absolute 5 min request deadline with a 5 min idle timeout, reject
    target ports outside 1..65535 with 400.
  * SOCKS5: 30 s handshake timeout.
  * New MAX_CONNECTIONS (default 4096) limit on concurrent client
    connections.
  * Keys: an unreadable key is an error instead of a reason to generate a
    new one; ssh_key.pub is always derived from ssh_key; atomic writes.
  * Status: no TCP probes to sshd while the session is up.
  * Reject an IPv6 SSH_HOST at startup: the tunnel connects over IPv4 only.
  * postinst: remove only /etc/defaults/ssh-gate, not the whole directory.
  * Harden the systemd unit (system call filter, ProtectProc, ProtectClock,
    ProtectHostname, ProtectKernelLogs, MemoryDenyWriteExecute).

 -- Nikita Kozlov <niakrisn@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:57:27 +0000

ssh-gate (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Support multiple listen addresses for the SOCKS5 and HTTP proxies:
    SOCKS5_LISTEN and HTTP_LISTEN now accept a comma-separated list,
    one proxy server per address.
  * Reject listen addresses without a port: an empty port made
    net.Listen bind to a random ephemeral port.

 -- Nikita Kozlov <niakrisn@gmail.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:06:41 +0300

ssh-gate (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Self-heal dead SSH links, correct routing, bounded shutdown.
  * Ship the config as /etc/default/ssh-gate and migrate the old
    /etc/defaults/ssh-gate on upgrade.

